{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 982 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fdb582283e016798869c3be5f5046598d609856e7a7a826303cd932cb98cd9d2" :edb/db-before-t 981 :edb/db-after-t 982 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534294 50 #inst "2026-10-06T15:39:25.385Z" 13194139534294 true] [17592186152105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283249 13194139534294 true] [17592186152105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283253 13194139534294 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283242 13194139534294 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283246 13194139534294 true] [17592186152695 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534294 true] [17592186152695 1100 "Consider the line $x = 5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$?" 13194139534294 false] [17592186152695 1100 "Consider the line $x=5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186152695 1145 "First, notice that the line $x=5$ passes through the points $A(5,0)$ and $B(5,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(-4,1).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1-0}{-4-(-5)}(x-(-5)) \\\\ y & =x+5 \\\\ x-y+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283243 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1089 "q-281140" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1100 "Consider the line $y=2x-3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=12.$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1113 #uuid "87e8ce2c-dfcb-53fd-8d39-6e18379846c0" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283242 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=2x-3$ passes through the points $A(0,-3)$ and $B(1,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(0,-6)$ and ${B}^{′}(2,-1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{-1+6}{2-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{5}{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =\\frac{5}{2}x \\\\ 2y+12 & =5x \\\\ 5x-2y & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283244 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283245 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1041 "field-1" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283245 13194139534294 true] [17592186283243 1110 #uuid "0515d3d5-630a-5eec-b3d6-9d7749d7bcd9" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283244 1034 "2x-5y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534294 true] [17592186283244 1111 #uuid "d84c2a45-c2f3-5cf2-b567-295b70a67bba" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283245 1034 "5x-2y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534294 true] [17592186283245 1111 #uuid "813777da-7c21-5540-9d09-57659feecf69" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283247 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1089 "q-281236" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1100 "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=15.$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1113 #uuid "6e5a2374-c8a0-52ba-8347-79e5368d0c7b" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283246 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+1$ passes through the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(3,2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 16 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(2,-1)$ and ${B}^{′}(16,7).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{7-(-1)}{16-2}(x-2) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{8}{14}(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\frac{4}{7}(x-2) \\\\ 7y+7 & =4x-8 \\\\ 4x-7y & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283248 13194139534294 true] [17592186283247 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534294 true] [17592186283247 1041 "field-1" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283247 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283248 13194139534294 true] [17592186283247 1110 #uuid "e5705ca9-05be-5a28-b721-a34551083b33" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283248 1034 "4x-7y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534294 true] [17592186283248 1111 #uuid "48876e20-f769-587d-899b-e540c2004f7d" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283250 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1089 "q-281580" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1100 "Consider the line $y=-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-8.$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1113 #uuid "a2bac187-b724-5e7f-a90f-46647a5ab6f9" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283249 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=-1$ passes through the points $P(0,-1)$ and $Q(1,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(0,2)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,3).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{3-2}{4-0}(x-0) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{4}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-8 & =x \\\\ x-4y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283251 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283252 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1041 "field-1" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283251 13194139534294 true] [17592186283250 1110 #uuid "8aa02b0c-8b31-5c64-9b56-9d19ff5fb2b1" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283251 1034 "x-4y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534294 true] [17592186283251 1111 #uuid "9038b770-629c-59e3-846f-cd94357fe89e" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283252 1034 "4x-y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534294 true] [17592186283252 1111 #uuid "fbe94949-ee3d-5dc9-ac5e-b63612d0d720" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283254 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1089 "q-281581" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1100 "Consider the line $y=3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=21.$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1113 #uuid "e4819488-a7a0-5944-ad18-73e05d2e8341" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283253 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=3$ passes through the points $P(0,3)$ and $Q(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,3)$ and ${Q}^{′}(10,1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1-3}{10-9}(x-9) \\\\ y-3 & =-2(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-2x+18 \\\\ 2x+y & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283255 13194139534294 true] [17592186283254 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534294 true] [17592186283254 1041 "field-1" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283254 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283255 13194139534294 true] [17592186283254 1110 #uuid "5f103862-4811-51d6-85cd-845062526155" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283255 1034 "2x+y" 13194139534294 true] [17592186283255